Benchmark data licensing
========================

The polyvoice source is MIT. The DATASETS used by this benchmark are NOT MIT and
keep their own licenses. This repository does NOT redistribute any dataset audio
— the scripts under ../scripts/ download it on demand from the original sources,
and benchmark/manifests/*.json store only file-id lists and provenance, not
audio. Reference RTTM annotations, where checked in under ../data/, retain the
license of their source corpus.

VoxConverse (dev / test)
  Source:  https://github.com/joonson/voxconverse
  Paper:   Chung et al., "Spot the conversation: speaker diarisation in the wild",
           Interspeech 2020 (arXiv:2007.01216)
  Annotations: CC-BY-4.0 (VoxConverse RTTMs).
  Audio:   sourced from YouTube; governed by YouTube's terms — NOT redistributed
           here. Download via scripts/download-voxconverse-{dev,test}.sh.

AMI Meeting Corpus (test split, Mix-Headset)
  Source:  https://groups.inf.ed.ac.uk/ami/corpus/
  License: CC-BY-4.0.
  Audio:   downloaded via scripts/download-ami-test.sh — NOT redistributed here.

Competitor model weights
  pyannote/speaker-diarization-3.1 and its sub-models are gated on Hugging Face
  (license acceptance + access token); they are downloaded by the user, never
  vendored. Other competitor weights follow their respective upstream licenses.

Attribution
  When citing numbers produced by this harness, cite the dataset (VoxConverse /
  AMI / NOTSOFAR-1) and disclose the collar and overlap-handling, per
  docs/BENCHMARKS.md.

NOTSOFAR-1 (dev-set-1, single-channel)
  Source:  https://huggingface.co/datasets/microsoft/NOTSOFAR
           (mirror of the Azure blob original at notsofarsa.blob.core.windows.net)
  Paper:   CHiME-8 DASR challenge (arXiv:2407.16447)
  Split:   benchmark-datasets/dev_set/240825.1_dev1 — 36 meetings, first sorted
           single-channel sc_* device per meeting; GT gt_transcription.json
           converted to RTTM by ../scripts/notsofar-to-rttm.py.
  License: CC-BY-4.0 (see the dataset's DATA_LICENSE file).
